[INTENT]
Purpose: Grant CREATE ASSERTION to ROAD_KIT_DEV, so the spec patch 07 backport
  (build-plan-08 phase 2) can create road_reserved_composition and road_admin_reachable.
Approach: Single least-privilege grant from the ADB ADMIN connection, then read back
  DBA_SYS_PRIVS to prove it landed. Mirrors the line in admin/grant-schema-privileges.sql,
  copied from road-cal in this phase, which is the reproducible source of truth.
Reason: Without it deploy/create/96_assertions.sql fails with ORA-01031. road-cal took the
  same grant on 2026-08-19 (road-cal logs/admin/runs/20260819_103835_grant-assertion-privilege).
  This is build-plan-08 phase 0, which exists precisely to front-load the one step needing
  elevated credentials.
Expected objects: none created. One system privilege granted.
Risk: Low. CREATE ASSERTION is schema-scoped -- it permits constraining this schema's own
  tables only. Deliberately NOT CREATE ANY ASSERTION, which would reach other schemas.
Prior history checked: road-kit has never been granted this privilege; the identical grant to
  ROAD_CAL_SCHEMA is the only prior instance in any environment.
[END INTENT]

